    <exercise workspace="2.0in">
      <p>
        Because of inflation, the current price of eggs is 180% of the price last year. 
        If the current price of eggs is $3.18 (per dozen), what was the price of eggs last year? [In other words, 3.18 is 180% of what?]
      </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="2.0in">
      <p>
        A jacket originally cost $40. Then it was marked down to 60% of its original price. What is the new price? [In other words, what is 60% of 40?]
      </p>
    </exercise>
    <exercise workspace="2.0in">
      <p>
        An exam is worth 42 points. A student earns 37 points. What is their score as a percent? [In other words, 27 is what percent of 42?]
      </p>
    </exercise>
